2 CONT
2 CONT Firma Berner i Helsinki:   http://eng.berner.fi/company/history
2 CONT
2 CONT The story of Berner started in the 1880s, when the young Norwegian Sören Berner arrived in Helsinki in order to chart the markets in this town of 40,000. He decided to start business operations in Finland by importing herring dire
2 CONC ctly to Helsinki from the fishing port in Stavanger. As trading activity increased, Berner added other fish products to his wholesale trade range. The first wheat flour deliveries from America led to agency sales. In addition to s
2 CONC alt, rye, barley, and fish products, Berner began to import rarer delicacies such as marzipan, liquorice, raisins, and coffee. (Look at the link.)
