1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ludvig Molvig May 11, 1988|The Morning Call Ludvig Molvig, 66, of 1381 Bonnie Ave., Hanover Township, Lehigh County, died Tuesday in Muhlenberg Hospital Center. He was the husband of Gilda M. (Martin) Molvig.
2 CONT
2 CONT A 1944 graduate of Cornell University, he was a metallurgical engineer for Bethlehem Steel Corp. for 28 years before retiring in 1977.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Oslo, Norway, he was a son of the late Ludvig and Ruth (Berner) Molvig. He served in the Army Signal Corps during World War II.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving with his widow are a son, Dr. Kim of Boston, Mass.; a sister, Mrs. Phillip Landis of Milwaukee, Wis.; his stepmother, Agnes Molvig of Brooklyn, N.Y., and two grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be at 4 p.m. Thursday in the Long Funeral Home, 500 Linden St., Bethlehem. A calling hour will precede the services.
