2 CONT
2 CONT Rolf Brostrup Berner (20 June 1894 Helsinki, Finland - August 26, 1978 Lahti) was the Progressive Party Member of Parliament from 1945 to 1951 and he was elected from the Kymi constituency. Berner's parents were merchant Sören Ber
2 CONC ner and Bertha Lagus. Berner was awarded the commercial counselor's title in 1954. Deputy Director, Sören Berner & Co., later Berner Ltd, Managing Director 1920-1958, Chairman of the Board 1945-1978 Service of the Ministry of the 
2 CONC People's Trade Commissioner in 1939, the commercial department manager from 1939 to 1941, Liinahamari sea transportation committee member 1940-1941 The presidential elections of 1940, 1943, 1950 (National Progressive Party) Libera
2 CONC l Union Vice-President Owned a farm Heinolan rural municipality One of the founding members of Liberal International
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://fi.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolf_B._Berner
2 CONT
2 CONT http://runeberg.org/kuka/1978/0079.html
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fi.billiongraves.international/grave/Rolf-Brostrup-Berner/34349097
